SARAH 128 - KEY HELP
===================

CS = CAPS SHIFT, SS = SYMBOL SHIFT
BREAK = CS+SPACE, DELETE = CS+0
Arrows: CS+5 left, CS+8 right, CS+7 up, CS+6 down.

1) WITHOUT AN FTP CONNECTION
---------------------------
Settings and local functions do not need an FTP login.
L and SS+L start the connection rather than require one.

F           Set the default file name for SS+D
T           Set file start address (BS-DOS, not ESXDOS)
SS+T        Toggle deletion of the original TAP (BS-DOS)
CS+T        Toggle Run after TAP extraction (BS-DOS)
A           Toggle automatic login when Sarah starts
H           Set FTP host
E           Set user name
P           Set password
SS+P        Toggle password visibility
N           Select LIST / NLST for the next directory read
SS+N        Select abbreviated / full listing
W           Set Wi-Fi on/off when quitting Sarah
V           Save the complete application with its settings
Q           Quit; Wi-Fi state follows W
G           Choose a local CFG profile
K           Read local sara.hlp
L           Start manual login; enter user and password
SS+L (=)    Start automatic login using configured values
CS+L        Not assigned in the main screen

TAP OPTIONS (BS-DOS)
-------------------
TAP files are always downloaded and extracted.
Delete=Y deletes the original TAP after extraction.
Run=Y starts the extracted program; Run=N returns to Sarah.
The extracted files are kept in both cases.
Options appear on the second row from the bottom when idle.
V saves these settings with the application.

CACHED DIRECTORY (NO FTP COMMANDS)
---------------------------------
These keys need a directory already loaded into memory.

Up / Down   Move the cursor
Left/Right  Change directory page
SPACE       Toggle the current item's mark, then move down
CS+M        Mark all real items (except the parent '..')
SS+M (.)    Unmark all items
I           Find text in names and mark matching items
            Searching replaces the previous marks
J           Jump to item number (1-65535), BREAK cancels
            Invalid or out-of-range numbers leave the cursor
            Current number appears at the right of File/Start
X           Enter long-name scrolling (X right, Z left)

LONG FILE NAMES
---------------
Extensions of 1-3 characters stay in a fixed right column.
X/Z scroll only the body; '..' means more text to the right.
Longer extensions scroll with the entire original name.
X           Start scrolling a name longer than the row
X / Z       Scroll the name right / left
Other key   Leave scrolling and perform that key's action
Z opens text only outside long-name scrolling.

TEXT VIEWER (AFTER LOADING)
--------------------------
Left        Previous screen
Right       Next screen
BREAK       Return to Sarah

ENTER opens TXT and POK files in the same viewer.
For CFG or other files, use Z.
Viewing downloads into memory; it does not save a file.
Non-printable bytes appear as dots. TAB is one space.
Files over 65535 bytes are shown only up to that limit.
A warning is displayed before downloading a large file.

INPUT EDITOR
------------
Left/Right  Move the cursor
CS+0        Backspace: delete before the cursor
CS+9        Delete the character at the cursor
CS+1 (EDIT) Clear the whole input field
ENTER       Accept the value, regardless of cursor position
BREAK      Cancel and keep the previous value
CS+3        Also cancels input

2) WITH AN FTP CONNECTION
------------------------
These operations communicate with the FTP server.
No directory is needed to enter a file name manually.

O           Log off
S           Show file size; enter the name
U           Upload a local file; enter its name
CS+D        Download a file by entering its name
SS+D        Download the default file
C           Send an FTP command
R           Read the directory again
7           Create a directory

WITH A LOADED DIRECTORY
-----------------------
ENTER       Open directory or supported file under cursor
ESXDOS      TAP/SNA/Z80/TRD/SCL launch after downloading
            SNAPLOAD and VDISK commands must be installed
BREAK       Go to the parent directory
D           Download marked files, or the item under cursor
6           Rename the item
DELETE      Delete marked items, or the item under cursor
Y / N       Confirm / cancel deletion
Z           Download any file for viewing as text

D and DELETE use marks first; without marks they use cursor.

DURING TRANSFERS
----------------
B           Abort a running file download or upload
BREAK       Interrupt directory reception

CFG PROFILE SELECTION
-----------------------------
G           Open the profile list
Up / Down   Preview and select a profile
ENTER       Keep the profile and perform SS+L login
BREAK       Restore the previous profile; do not log in
If connected elsewhere, SS+L can ask about reconnecting.
Y           Reconnect when asked
N / B       Decline reconnecting

UPLOAD CHOICES
--------------
O           Overwrite the existing file
A           Append to the existing file
N           Create a new file using STOU
CS+1 (EDIT) Cancel the file-exists choice
B           Abort
Upload is still under development.

OPENING FILES (BS-DOS)
---------------------
ENTER on TAP downloads and extracts the program.
Delete and Run follow SS+T / CS+T settings above.
ENTER on SNA / Z80 downloads and hands it to the NMI menu.
An unsupported NMI menu shows a message and returns.
ENTER also previews supported 6144/6912-byte screen files.
Press a new key to leave the screen preview.

Keep sara.hlp next to sara.cfg on the current disk.
Press K to open it, Left/Right to browse and BREAK to return.
